<standOff type="notes1" corresp="#TNV4"><note xml:lang="ta" target="#kar"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. TP6n:</term> kāru mālaiyu mullai kuṟiñci | kūtir yāma meṉmaṉār pulavar ||</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#munpani"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. TP7n:</term> paṉiyetir paruvamu muritteṉa moḻipa ||</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#venil"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. TP9n:</term> naṭuvunilait tiṇaiyē naṇpakala vēṉiloṭu | muṭivunilai maruṅkiṉ muṉṉiya neṟittē ||</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#pani"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. TP10n:</term> piṉpaṉi tāṉu muritteṉa moḻipa ||</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#kutir"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 23:</term> kuṟiñcikku… poḻutu kūtirum yāmamum muṉpaṉiyum.</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#venil"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 23:</term> pālaikku… poḻutu naṇpakalum vēṉilum piṉpaṉiyum.</note>
<note xml:lang="ta" target="#kar"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 24:</term> mullaikku… poḻutu kārum mālaiyum.</note>
</standOff>
<standOff type="notes4" corresp="#TNV4"><note xml:lang="en" target="#polute">Nakkīrar states that since Tolkāppiyar does not assign seasons to <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">marutam</hi></term> and <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">neytal</hi></term>, all six are appropriate – IAC 1, p. 25: <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">maruttatiṟkum neytaṟkum perumpoḻutu colliṟṟiṉmaiyiṉ aṟuvakai yirutuvum uriyaveṉakkoḷka</hi></q>.</note>
<note xml:lang="en" target="#polute">The <foreign xml:lang="ta-Latn">Tolkāppiyam</foreign> treats these slightly differently. Poetic settings and their appropriate season and time of day are listed in separate <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>-s. This is also why there is significant overlap with the list of sources for the next <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>. The TP also has a different list from that found here. Only <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">kuṟiñci</hi></term>, <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">pālai</hi></term>, and <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">mullai</hi></term> have prescribed seasons, and only five seasons are listed – <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">kūtir</hi></term> and <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">[muṉ]paṉi</hi></term> (<term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">kuṟiñci</hi></term>); <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">vēṉil</hi></term> and <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">piṉpaṉi</hi></term> (<term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">pālai</hi></term>); and <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">kār</hi></term> (<term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">mullai</hi></term>).</note></standOff>
